cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use ER2 in your work, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Please also cite PARI/GP and SymPy, which ER2 builds on.
type: software
title: "ER2: Mathematical Python"
abstract: >-
  ER2 is a superset of Python for mathematics. It adds symbolic syntax
  (sym x, x^2), exact arithmetic by default, and computational number theory
  through PARI/GP (via cypari2) and SymPy. The whole Python ecosystem stays
  available, and ER2 code runs in Jupyter and Quarto. It is named after
  the mathematician Paul Erdős.
authors:
  - alias: eph
version: 0.4.1
repository-code: "https://github.com/oeistools/ER2"
url: "https://github.com/oeistools/ER2"
license: MIT
keywords:
